{
  "about": "The module-by-module sound tests (journal 2026-11-26, \"A new approach: one module, one effect at a time\"). For each GP-200 effect whose GP-50 copy is another effect: the GP-50 effects to hear it against, on the GP-200 alone. Used by tools/sound-tests.js. Effects are named as Valeton's files name them: the tested effect by its GP-200 name, the alternatives and the chain by their GP-50 names (each must be an effect the GP-200 also has, at the same code). The map's current pick is added by the tool as B (unless it is a stand-in, or the GP-200 lacks it); \"alts\" are the others, picked by Claude by kind (maker, gain, speaker layout, sort of effect), up to 3 in all. \"chain\" names the neutral chain the test plays through: the tested module replaces that chain's module of the same name, everything else off. \"notTested\": effects left out of the listening, with the reason.",
